        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_1247"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A blood coagulation disease that is characterized by easy bleeding, has_symptom prolonged umbilical cord bleeding, epistaxis, bleeding of the gums, menorrhagia, recurrent miscarriages, abnormal scar formation and wound healing, and hemarthrosis, and has_material_basis_in autosomal recessive inheritance of mutation of the F13A1 or F13B gene, which encodes Factor XIII, formally known as fibrin stabilizing factor.</obo:IAO_0000115>
