        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_936"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A brain disease that is characterized by low pressure inside the skull, and thus in the brain tissue and cerebrospinal fluid; may occur as a result of an occult or iatrogenically caused leak of CSF into another body cavity; may result in the downward displacement of the cerebellar tonsils through the foramen magnum or Chiari malformation; has_symptom orthostatic headache; other symptoms are related to compression of cranial nerves due to brain sagging.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/doid.owl"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MESH:D019585</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
